{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","<div align=\"center\">\n","\n","<img src=\"https://capsule-render.vercel.app/api?type=waving&color=0:050B18,50:0B3D91,100:123B60&height=190&section=header&text=Luis%20Barahona&fontSize=42&fontColor=FFFFFF&fontAlignY=38&desc=DATA%20ENGINEERING%20%7C%20ARTIFICIAL%20INTELLIGENCE%20%7C%20DEVELOPER&descAlignY=62&descSize=14\" width=\"50%\" alt=\"Luis Barahona MX- Data Engineering and AI\">\n","\n","<img src=\"https://readme-typing-svg.demolab.com?font=Fira+Code&weight=500&size=17&duration=3500&pause=1200&color=38BDF8&center=true&vCenter=true&width=600&lines=Python+%7C+SQL+%7C+Data+Engineering;Artificial+Intelligence+%7C+Machine+Learning;Data+Science+%7C+Cloud+Computing;Building+Technology+for+the+Future\" alt=\"Technical expertise\">\n","\n","</div>\n","\n","---\n","<div align=\"center\">\n","### Professional Profile\n","\n","I am a Mexican Data Engineer and a 2026 graduate of Universidad del Caribe, passionate about technology, innovation, and continuous learning.\n","Beyond technical expertise, I value communication, teamwork, collaboration, and building meaningful connections with others. I believe that every person offers an opportunity to learn something new, and I am always motivated to share knowledge, explore new ideas, and grow both personally and professionally.\n","\n","---\n","\n","<div align=\"center\">\n","\n","<img src=\"https://skillicons.dev/icons?i=python,mysql,postgres,git,github,react,firebase,linux,docker,vscode&theme=dark\" alt=\"Technical skills\">\n","\n","\n","<strong>Data Engineering ·  Data Analytics · Data science · Artificial Intelligence · Machine Learning · Data Analytics · Developer</strong>\n","\n","</div>\n","\n","---\n","<div align=\"center\">\n","\n","| Platform | Contact |\n","|:---|:---|\n","| Email | [190300395@ucaribe.edu.mx](mailto:190300395@ucaribe.edu.mx) |\n","| GitHub | [github.com/LuisBarahonaMX](https://github.com/LuisBarahonaMX) |\n","| LinkedIn | [linkedin.com/in/luis-barahona-mx](https://www.linkedin.com/in/luis-barahona-mx/) |\n","| Instagram | [@luisbarahonamx](https://www.instagram.com/luisbarahonamx/) |\n","| X | [@luisbarahonaMX](https://x.com/luisbarahonaMX) |\n","| Website | [SIKO AI Platform](https://sikoai.web.app/) |\n","</div>\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"0wwJcFJeFqab"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"75RZwvBE4VSP"},"source":["{`# Clasificación de Desarrolladores de GitHub mediante Teoría de Grafos y Machine Learning\n","\n","### Análisis de redes sociales, extracción de características topológicas y clasificación supervisada\n","\n","**Área:** Ciencia de Datos | Machine Learning | Teoría de Grafos | Social Network Analysis  \n","**Lenguaje:** Python  \n","**Entorno:** Jupyter Notebook | Google Colab\n","\n","---\n","\n","## Descripción del proyecto\n","\n","Este notebook desarrolla un análisis de una red social de desarrolladores de **GitHub**, utilizando teoría de grafos y algoritmos de aprendizaje automático para explorar la clasificación de usuarios según su especialidad: **desarrollo web o Machine Learning**.\n","\n","El proyecto utiliza el conjunto de datos **MUSAE GitHub**, que contiene información sobre desarrolladores, sus conexiones y etiquetas de especialización.\n","\n","El objetivo es estudiar cómo las características estructurales de una red social pueden utilizarse para identificar patrones de conexión y construir modelos de clasificación supervisada.\n","\n","## Objetivos\n","\n","- Construir una red dirigida de desarrolladores mediante NetworkX.\n","- Analizar nodos, aristas y relaciones entre usuarios.\n","- Calcular métricas de centralidad, conectividad y agrupamiento.\n","- Explorar métricas de predicción de enlaces, como Jaccard, Adamic-Adar y Preferential Attachment.\n","- Limpiar e integrar los conjuntos de datos de conexiones, características y etiquetas.\n","- Dividir los datos en entrenamiento (60%), validación (20%) y prueba (20%).\n","- Implementar modelos supervisados utilizando LinearSVC y XGBoost.\n","- Explorar la optimización de hiperparámetros mediante GridSearchCV.\n","- Evaluar los modelos mediante Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1-Score y ROC-AUC.\n","\n","## Metodología\n","\n","El ejercicio sigue una estructura basada en **CRISP-DM**, comenzando con la exploración y preparación de tres archivos: `musae_git_edges.csv`, `musae_git_features.csv` y `musae_git_target.csv`.\n","\n","Posteriormente, se construye una red mediante NetworkX y se calculan métricas topológicas para caracterizar las relaciones entre desarrolladores.\n","\n","Se exploran técnicas de preprocesamiento, integración de datos y construcción de variables para entrenar modelos de clasificación supervisada.\n","\n","Finalmente, se implementan procedimientos de validación y comparación entre LinearSVC y XGBoost para analizar su capacidad de clasificación.\n","\n","## Tecnologías utilizadas\n","\n","**Python | Pandas | NumPy | NetworkX | Scikit-learn | XGBoost | Matplotlib | Jupyter Notebook**\n","\n","## Aplicaciones\n","\n","Este proyecto demuestra cómo la teoría de grafos y el aprendizaje automático pueden combinarse para analizar comunidades digitales, identificar patrones de interacción y explorar la clasificación de usuarios a partir de sus relaciones dentro de una red.\n","\n","**Alcance:** Notebook académico y experimental. La evaluación definitiva de los modelos requiere completar y verificar la integración de métricas, el preprocesamiento y las pruebas sobre datos no utilizados durante el entrenamiento.\n","\n","---\n","\n","**Autor:** Data Engineer Luis Barahona  \n","**Institución:** Universidad del Caribe, México  \n","**GitHub:** [LuisBarahonaMX](https://github.com/LuisBarahonaMX)\n","\n","**Categoría:** Graph Machine Learning | Network Analysis | Node Classification | Data Science`}"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"QoRYoAmsJirw"},"source":["#<font color=\"red\">EXPLORACIÓN DE LOS DATOS\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"iFFqQZYr0fMU"},"outputs":[],"source":["# ————— Librerías —————\n","import networkx as nx\n","import pandas as pd\n","import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import json\n","import operator\n","\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"3PboMusT0fXF"},"outputs":[],"source":["\n","\n","# ————— Rutas de los datos —————\n","edges_path    = 'musae_git_edges.csv'    # aristas (sigue)\n","features_path = 'musae_git_features.csv' # atributos de los nodos\n","target_path   = 'musae_git_target.csv'   # etiquetas (web vs. ML)\n","\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"8fgGTv121wsv"},"outputs":[],"source":["# ————— Carga de los datos —————\n","edges_df    = pd.read_csv(edges_path)\n","features_df = pd.read_csv(features_path, index_col=0)\n","target_df   = pd.read_csv(target_path, index_col=0)\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":20,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747059335264,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"},"user_tz":300},"id":"o7tVAInP2R6C","outputId":"93eb664d-6660-41a5-9f72-154b56996ae2"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Aristas (edges): (289003, 2)\n","Atributos (features): (690374, 1)\n","Etiquetas (target): (37700, 2)\n"]}],"source":["\n","# ————— Descripción básica —————\n","print(\"Aristas (edges):\", edges_df.shape)\n","print(\"Atributos (features):\", features_df.shape)\n","print(\"Etiquetas (target):\", target_df.shape)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Q8SlDLQkJojj"},"source":["#<font color=\"red\">PREPOSESAMIENTO\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"2yCG8meN2a2h"},"source":["### ————— Construcción del grafo dirigido —————\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":1105,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747059605954,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"},"user_tz":300},"id":"kuxgvZKM2Teq","outputId":"a2acae85-b9cc-4532-c80b-9a363884c2fd"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Número de nodos en la red social: 37700\n","Número de aristas ('sigue'): 289003\n"]}],"source":["import pandas as pd\n","import networkx as nx\n","\n","# Rutas de los datos\n","edges_path = 'musae_git_edges.csv'\n","\n","# Cargar aristas\n","edges_df = pd.read_csv(edges_path)\n","\n","# Construcción del grafo dirigido usando los nombres correctos\n","G = nx.from_pandas_edgelist(\n","    edges_df,\n","    source='id_1',\n","    target='id_2',\n","    create_using=nx.DiGraph()\n",")\n","\n","# Conteo de nodos y aristas\n","print(\"Número de nodos en la red social:\", G.number_of_nodes())\n","print(\"Número de aristas ('sigue'):\", G.number_of_edges())\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"eZJWYYJq5bb9"},"source":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"dd4grSRu5GgU"},"source":["## Caracteriza a cada nodo a partir de métricas adecuadas (métricas asociadas al grafo). Emplea la mayor cantidad de métricas para asegurarte de caractaerizar de la mejro manera a los nodos."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"fKO5AYjg5a_5"},"source":["# Predicción de enlaces\n","\n","Dado un par de nodos, $A$ y $B$ (**no conectados**), buscamos predecir si en el futuro ambos estarán conectados. Podemos usar como predictores diferentes medidas que caracterizan a ambos nodos algunas de las cuales se discutirán en este documento.\n","\n","\n","## Vecinos comunes\n","\n","\n","$$\\text{comm_neigh}(A, B) = |N(A)\\cap N(B)|$$"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"HvIhr_4k6_Cg"},"outputs":[],"source":["# ————— 1) Preparar vecinos como conjuntos —————\n","# Trabajamos sobre la versión no dirigida para métricas de enlace\n","U = G.to_undirected()\n","neighbors = {n: set(U.neighbors(n)) for n in U.nodes()}\n","\n","# ————— 2) Generar pares positivos y negativos acotados —————\n","pos_pairs = list(U.edges())  # pares que ya existen\n","\n","# Para negativos: por cada nodo muestreamos hasta k pares de segundo orden\n","import random\n","neg_pairs = []\n","k = 5  # número de contrapartes negativas por nodo\n","\n","for u in U.nodes():\n","    # vecinos de segundo orden: union de vecinos de los vecinos, excluyendo vecinos directos y u\n","    soc = set().union(*(neighbors[w] for w in neighbors[u])) - neighbors[u] - {u}\n","    # muestreamos k candidatos\n","    sampled = random.sample(list(soc), min(k, len(soc)))\n","    for v in sampled:\n","        if not U.has_edge(u, v):\n","            neg_pairs.append((u, v))\n","\n","# Ebunch con positivos y negativos\n","ebunch = pos_pairs + neg_pairs\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":16801,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747060638842,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"},"user_tz":300},"id":"Bfhy-3Lo7XaA","outputId":"60abb9f3-2171-472f-c00c-626d2064f471"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Common Neighbors: [((0, 23977), 0), ((23977, 30863), 3), ((23977, 29826), 1), ((23977, 31890), 11), ((23977, 17127), 2)]\n","Jaccard: [((0, 23977), 0.0), ((23977, 30863), 0.03225806451612903), ((23977, 29826), 0.027777777777777776), ((23977, 31890), 0.0011604599641312375), ((23977, 17127), 0.02666666666666667)]\n","Adamic–Adar: [((0, 23977), 0), ((23977, 30863), 0.5191811381526727), ((23977, 29826), 0.10923450810153484), ((23977, 31890), 2.801074248933634), ((23977, 17127), 0.6676014366523757)]\n","Pref. Attach.: [((0, 23977), 32), ((23977, 30863), 2048), ((23977, 29826), 160), ((23977, 31890), 302656), ((23977, 17127), 1440)]\n"]}],"source":["# ————— 3) Calcular métricas de enlace solo para ebunch usando sets —————\n","import math\n","\n","cn_scores    = {}\n","jacc_scores  = {}\n","aa_scores    = {}\n","pa_scores    = {}\n","\n","for u, v in ebunch:\n","    Nu = neighbors[u]\n","    Nv = neighbors[v]\n","    inter = Nu & Nv\n","    union = Nu | Nv\n","\n","    cn_scores[(u, v)]   = len(inter)\n","    jacc_scores[(u, v)] = len(inter) / len(union) if union else 0.0\n","    aa_scores[(u, v)]   = sum(1/math.log(len(neighbors[w]))\n","                               for w in inter\n","                               if len(neighbors[w]) > 1)\n","    pa_scores[(u, v)]   = len(Nu) * len(Nv)\n","\n","# Ejemplo: ver primeras 5 puntuaciones\n","print(\"Common Neighbors:\", list(cn_scores.items())[:5])\n","print(\"Jaccard:\",         list(jacc_scores.items())[:5])\n","print(\"Adamic–Adar:\",     list(aa_scores.items())[:5])\n","print(\"Pref. Attach.:\",   list(pa_scores.items())[:5])\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"tyU691UW5e4M"},"source":["# Coeficiente de Jaccard\n","\n","$$\\text{jacc_coeff}(A, B) = \\frac{|N(A)\\cap N(B)|}{|N(A)\\cup N(B)|}$$"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":3682,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747060745314,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"},"user_tz":300},"id":"B1bpRYYq70oq","outputId":"cf3df4f2-a05e-44e1-a18b-e0f9ecef7de8"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["(0, 23977): 0.0000\n","(23977, 30863): 0.0323\n","(23977, 29826): 0.0278\n","(23977, 31890): 0.0012\n","(23977, 17127): 0.0267\n"]}],"source":["# ————— 1) Precomputar vecinos como conjuntos (en grafo no dirigido) —————\n","U = G.to_undirected()\n","neighbors = {n: set(U.neighbors(n)) for n in U.nodes()}\n","\n","# ————— 2) Definir ebunch (por ejemplo, aristas existentes + muestras negativas) —————\n","# ya deberías tenerlo en una lista `ebunch`\n","\n","# ————— 3) Cálculo manual y rápido de Jaccard —————\n","jacc_scores = {}\n","for u, v in ebunch:\n","    Nu, Nv = neighbors[u], neighbors[v]\n","    inter_size = len(Nu & Nv)\n","    # |union| = |Nu| + |Nv| - |intersection|\n","    union_size = len(Nu) + len(Nv) - inter_size\n","    jacc_scores[(u, v)] = inter_size / union_size if union_size else 0.0\n","\n","# ————— 4) Ejemplo de salida —————\n","for pair, score in list(jacc_scores.items())[:5]:\n","    print(f\"{pair}: {score:.4f}\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"YYpTiKCM5fvU"},"source":["## Índice Adamic-Adar\n","\n","$$\\text{adamic}(A, B) = \\sum_{u \\in N(A)\\cap N(B)}\\frac{1}{log|N(u)|}$$\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":4599,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747060796616,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"},"user_tz":300},"id":"Fbh6Eyd25U9b","outputId":"d23dd3ae-9e10-4aa9-fc42-fcb5357addb4"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["(0, 23977): 0.0000\n","(23977, 30863): 0.0323\n","(23977, 29826): 0.0278\n","(23977, 31890): 0.0012\n","(23977, 17127): 0.0267\n"]}],"source":["# ————— 1) Precomputar vecinos como conjuntos (en grafo no dirigido) —————\n","U = G.to_undirected()\n","neighbors = {n: set(U.neighbors(n)) for n in U.nodes()}\n","\n","# ————— 2) Definir ebunch (por ejemplo, aristas existentes + muestras negativas) —————\n","# ya deberías tenerlo en una lista `ebunch`\n","\n","# ————— 3) Cálculo manual y rápido de Jaccard —————\n","jacc_scores = {}\n","for u, v in ebunch:\n","    Nu, Nv = neighbors[u], neighbors[v]\n","    inter_size = len(Nu & Nv)\n","    # |union| = |Nu| + |Nv| - |intersection|\n","    union_size = len(Nu) + len(Nv) - inter_size\n","    jacc_scores[(u, v)] = inter_size / union_size if union_size else 0.0\n","\n","# ————— 4) Ejemplo de salida —————\n","for pair, score in list(jacc_scores.items())[:5]:\n","    print(f\"{pair}: {score:.4f}\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"By-UPmJI5umd"},"source":["## Enlace preferencial\n","\n","$$\\text{pref_attach}(A, B) = |N(A)| \\times |N(B)|$$"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":1564,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747060920179,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"},"user_tz":300},"id":"O7AgNkla5WRN","outputId":"db415a34-6927-427b-8d07-c09a6f0ae055"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["(0, 23977): 32\n","(23977, 30863): 2048\n","(23977, 29826): 160\n","(23977, 31890): 302656\n","(23977, 17127): 1440\n"]}],"source":["# ————— 1) Precomputar grado de cada nodo en el grafo no dirigido —————\n","U = G.to_undirected()\n","degree_dict = dict(U.degree())\n","\n","# ————— 2) Calcular Preferential Attachment manualmente para ebunch —————\n","pa_scores = {\n","    (u, v): degree_dict[u] * degree_dict[v]\n","    for u, v in ebunch\n","}\n","\n","# ————— 3) Ejemplo de salida —————\n","for pair, score in list(pa_scores.items())[:5]:\n","    print(f\"{pair}: {score}\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"3Mmjc0Nz5uN3"},"source":["#Separa tus datos en subconjuntos de entrenamiento, validación y prueba (proporción 60-20-20)."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"jtbhIj389Ivk"},"outputs":[],"source":["# ————— Celda: Preparar full_df —————\n","\n","# Renombrar la columna objetivo a 'label' y asegurarnos de que es string o int\n","target_df = target_df.rename(columns={'target': 'label'})\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":1225,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747061927916,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"},"user_tz":300},"id":"R4LVVuB8-tVl","outputId":"5a5e6a67-3ae8-4bbc-cd25-69881299fba3"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["edges_df: (289003, 2)\n","features_df: (690374, 1)\n","target_df: (37700, 2)\n"]}],"source":["# ————— 1) Carga de los tr